---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Badge } from "@/components/ui/badge";
---

<Layout title="K3s platform testbeds — Vinicius Cerutti">
  <div class="w-[min(1120px,calc(100%-44px))] mx-auto">
    <main>
      <header class="page-header">
        <div class="kicker">operations</div>
        <h1 class="page-title">K3s platform testbeds</h1>
        <p class="page-sub">HA clusters, MetalLB, Traefik, GPU nodes, firewalld, and local Vagrant/libvirt environments for platform experiments.</p>
      </header>

      <section class="project-layout py-[clamp(48px,6vw,72px)]">
        <div class="project-main">
          <h2>Intent</h2>
          <p>
            Platform work needs somewhere to break things safely. The testbed environment
            serves as a local mirror of production topology: multi-node K3s clusters, real
            load balancer behavior via MetalLB, Traefik as the ingress controller, and GPU
            nodes for workload scheduling experiments. Local environments run on Vagrant and
            libvirt; bare-metal nodes run RHEL 9.
          </p>

          <h2>Cluster topology</h2>
          <p>
            The standard layout is a three-node HA control plane with embedded etcd, plus
            separate worker nodes — one or more with NVIDIA GPUs. MetalLB operates in
            L2 mode on a dedicated address pool, providing real LoadBalancer IPs without a
            cloud provider. Traefik handles ingress with TLS termination and routes traffic
            to services by hostname.
          </p>
          <p>
            Firewalld manages zone-based filtering between cluster, storage, and management
            networks. Getting zone assignments right for K3s flannel traffic and NodePort
            ranges is consistently the most friction-heavy part of initial cluster bring-up
            on RHEL 9.
          </p>

          <h2>GPU node wiring</h2>
          <p>
            GPU nodes require the NVIDIA container toolkit, the device plugin DaemonSet,
            and a RuntimeClass pointing to the <code>nvidia</code> runtime. The RuntimeClass
            must be set in the pod spec or the GPU is invisible to the scheduler. Cluster-level
            device discovery only works after the device plugin has fully initialized — a
            common source of confusion during initial setup.
          </p>
          <p>
            The testbed was used to validate the NVIDIA GPU operator approach before
            applying it to production workloads, and to produce the
            <a href="/notes/nvidia-runtimeclass-gpu-workloads/" class="inline-link">nvidia-runtimeclass write-up</a>.
          </p>

          <h2>What the testbed validated</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>MetalLB L2 announcement behavior — ARP gratuitous announcements and failover timing between nodes.</li>
            <li>Traefik TLS options and scanner expectations — reproducing cipher suite issues before touching production ingress.</li>
            <li>Firewalld zone and masquerade rules needed for flannel overlay traffic on RHEL 9.</li>
            <li>Certificate trust propagation — kubelet and containerd trust stores, and where TLS verification breaks for internal registries.</li>
            <li>GPU RuntimeClass scheduling — verifying workloads only land on nodes with the device plugin running.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <aside class="project-side">
          <h3>stack</h3>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-6">
            {["k3s", "rhel9", "metallb", "traefik", "nvidia", "vagrant", "libvirt"].map(t => <Badge variant="outline">{t}</Badge>)}
          </div>
          <h3>themes</h3>
          <p>HA cluster setup, bare-metal networking, GPU scheduling, ingress and TLS, firewall configuration.</p>
          <h3>related notes</h3>
          <p>
            <a href="/notes/k3s-tls-trust-errors/" class="side-link">k3s TLS trust errors →</a><br/>
            <a href="/notes/nvidia-runtimeclass-gpu-workloads/" class="side-link">nvidia runtimeclass →</a><br/>
            <a href="/notes/traefik-tls-options-scanner-expectations/" class="side-link">traefik TLS options →</a>
          </p>
          <a href="/projects/" class="back-link">← all projects</a>
        </aside>
      </section>
    </main>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .page-header {
    padding: clamp(64px, 8vw, 108px) 0 clamp(36px, 4vw, 52px);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); max-width: 820px;
  }
  .kicker {
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 18px;
  }
  .page-title {
    font-size: clamp(38px, 5.5vw, 68px); font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.065em; line-height: 0.97; margin: 0 0 18px; color: var(--foreground);
  }
  .page-sub { font-size: 19px; color: var(--muted-foreground); line-height: 1.55; margin: 0; }
  .project-layout { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 260px; gap: clamp(40px, 5vw, 64px); }
  .project-main h2 {
    margin: 36px 0 10px; font-size: 22px; font-weight: 650;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em; color: var(--foreground);
  }
  .project-main h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .project-main p, .project-main li { color: #c3cbd6; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.7; }
  .project-main ul { padding-left: 1.3rem; margin: 10px 0 18px; }
  .project-main li + li { margin-top: 7px; }
  .project-main code { color: #dfbb7f; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.88em; background: rgba(216,166,87,0.07); padding: 1px 5px; border-radius: 4px; }
  .inline-link { color: var(--link); }
  .inline-link:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .project-side { border-left: 1px solid var(--border); padding-left: 26px; padding-top: 4px; }
  .project-side h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em; color: var(--faint); margin: 0 0 12px;
  }
  .project-side h3 + h3, .project-side div + h3, .project-side p + h3 { margin-top: 28px; padding-top: 28px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .project-side p { font-size: 14px; color: var(--muted-foreground); line-height: 1.6; margin: 0 0 8px; }
  .side-link { color: var(--link); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12px; }
  .side-link:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .back-link { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12px; color: var(--link); display: block; margin-top: 28px; }
  .back-link:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  @media (max-width: 780px) {
    .project-layout { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .project-side { border-left: none; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); padding-left: 0; padding-top: 24px; }
  }
</style>
